## 🚨🚨 REVIEWER BANNER — v2 → v3 (DECISIVE wrong-transport correction)

A third cross-plan round (Claude's integrated `update-…-goose.md`, updated *after* my v2, with 3 fresh parallel source traces) surfaced a **load-bearing error in my v1 AND v2 that would have made the Problem-B fix edit dead code.** Re-verified against live source this round:

* **🔴 DECISIVE — Problem B targeted the WRONG SERVER.** My v1/v2 Commit 1 cited `agent_service_bridge.py` + `agent_websocket_routes.py` (the `/ws/agent` AF-webui transport). **OpenStartup chat does NOT use that transport.** The UI connects to **`/ws/manager`** (`useManagerChat.js:40`; `setupProxy.js:24` "Proxy ONLY /ws/manager"). The real emit sites are **`manager_websocket_routes.py`** + **`websocket_interactive.py`** + **`conversation_service.py`**. My v2's facts B-F2/F3/F4 (citing `agent_service_bridge.py`) are **wrong for the live chat** and are corrected below.
* **🔴 Problem B is HALF-wired, not absent.** `message_end` **already sends `message_id`** (`manager_websocket_routes.py:512-514`); the UI **already reads** `data.message_id` (`useManagerChat.js:384`) and the `pending_input` handler **already commits** the prior round's bubble (`:266`). What's missing: `token`/`pending_input`/`message_start` (in `websocket_interactive.py:201,214,314`) don't carry `message_id`, and the id isn't minted **per round**. Fix = finish the wiring + dedupe, NOT build from zero.
* **🟢 Reuse the existing round seam.** `conversational_inferencer.py:397` already fires `send_turn_boundary(...)` at iteration boundaries, and the UI has a `turn_boundary` handler (`useManagerChat.js:410`). Mint `{message_id, round_index}` at THIS seam — don't invent a new one.
* **🟢 Per-round View-Prompt gap closed (from Codex/X).** A single per-turn `turn.json` can't show round 2's prompt. Adopt **per-round artifacts** `turn_NNN/round_MMM/turn.json` + a `round` param on `get_turn_data`/REST/`ManagerChatView`. Resume is **message-based** (`session_routes.py:148`) so it's unaffected.

All Problem-A and Problem-C-1/C-2 findings from v2 survive (C already correctly targeted `conversation_service.py`/`session_store.py`). The transport correction only affects Problem B's commits + the §A1-B facts + §5 files. Full trail in §A4 v3 changelog; §A4.1 re-answers "pick one".

## REVIEWER BANNER — v1 → v2 (cross-plan integration; 3 corrections, 1 NEW sub-problem)

A peer-plan audit (Claude's `update-…-goose.md` — now on-topic and the strongest of the three; Codex's `codex/parallel_groups_assistant_rounds_turn_artifacts_plan.md` — conceptually good but **zero file:line citations**) surfaced findings my v1 got wrong or missed. All re-verified against live source:

* **CORRECTION (Problem A) — a tabbed widget ALREADY EXISTS; v1 was wrong to "build a new one".** `MultiInputWidget.js` (in `react-shared/src/inputs/`) is a tabbed compound widget that already exists — but it is **unreachable** (the dispatcher never routes to it) **and lossy** (it flattens `{choice_index, inputs}` to a scalar at `MultiInputWidget.js:59-69` and emits `{values}` at `:93`, dropping the typed-input plan's composite nested payload). The real blocker is `ConversationToolWidget.js:117` — a **hardcoded `if (metadata.compound) → CompoundWidget`** (the sequential "Step N of M" stepper at `:61`) that intercepts BEFORE the `widget_type` registry lookup at `:134`. **Fix = rewire the compound branch to a de-lossified `MultiInputWidget` (preserving raw child payloads), NOT build a new `CompoundTabbedInput`.** (Verified: ConversationToolWidget.js:61,117,134; MultiInputWidget.js:4,54-69,93.)
* **NEW SUB-PROBLEM C-2 (both my v1 AND Codex missed it).** The assistant response is **never persisted as its own message**, and the session index goes stale: `data_svc.append_message` (used by the WS route at `manager_websocket_routes.py:374`) → `session_store.append_message:334-345` calls `_persist_session` but **NOT `_update_index()`** → `sessions_index.message_count` stays `1` (this is the "1 msgs" you saw) while the header counted 3. Also `run_conversation_turn` blocks for the whole loop and appends **once** with `final_content` (`manager_websocket_routes.py:423,429`) — intermediate rounds never become their own messages. (Verified: session_store.py:334-345; data_service.py:670-671; manager_websocket_routes.py:374,423,429.)
* **MODEL UPGRADE — adopt the turn/round hierarchy.** v1's Problem-C fix was "remove the +1 anchor". The cleaner, more elegant model (from Claude's plan, verified compatible) is: **Turn = one user message + its complete response = one `turn_NNN/`; Round = one LLM iteration within a turn = `turn_NNN/round_MMM/`.** The AF `on_new_turn` callback is really a **round boundary**; OpenStartup must reinterpret it as "new round within the current user turn", not "new top-level turn". This single seam unifies B (per-round bubble), C-1 (no dir split), and C-2 (persist each round) — see §D7 (rewritten).

Everything in v1 that was correct (Problem B's "no `message_id`" diagnosis; the `parallel_group` int-not-bool contract; fix order B+C before A) survives. Full trail in §A4 v2 changelog; §A4.1 answers "pick one plan".

