### §A4.1 If forced to pick ONE plan among the 3 (v3 — answer CHANGED)

**Honest answer: Claude's `update-…-goose.md` (its latest, post-v2 version).** I'm changing my emphasis from v2 because this round it caught a **load-bearing error in my own plan**:

* **It alone targeted the right transport.** My v1 AND v2 aimed Problem B at `agent_service_bridge.py` / `/ws/agent` — a server **OpenStartup chat never uses**. Claude proved (and I re-verified: `useManagerChat.js:40`, `setupProxy.js:24`) the live transport is `/ws/manager`. My fix would have edited dead code and the overwrite bug would have persisted. That is the single most consequential correctness fact in this whole effort, and only Claude's plan had it right.
* **It also kept the best of all three:** the turn/round hierarchy (the unifying model), Problem C-2 (persist-each-round + `_update_index`), AND folded in Codex/X's per-round artifact metadata for View-Prompt — while staying source-anchored throughout.
* **Codex's plan** contributed the right *ideas* (implicit-group default, persist intermediate rounds, `parent_user_message_id`) but still has **no file:line citations** — not execution-grade alone.

**Honest caveat (unchanged):** my document has better *structure* (3-tier, risk register, numbered commits/tests). **v3 (this file) now folds Claude's transport correction + per-round-artifact adoption INTO that structure**, so to *execute from*, pick **v3**; for the best independent *analysis that caught my mistake*, Claude's plan earned it outright this round.
